==Enemy==
The main reason to get the [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]]. Star Peng is very threatening despite his Single Attack, as he pushes rapidly with his high DPS and a 100% chance to [[Warp|warp]] units back by 500 range for 3.3 seconds.

While Star Peng's base stats may look unimpressive, strength magnifications combined with insufficient Anti-Starred Alien Treasures can ramp up these peons' stats enough to make them almost unbeatable, even if you're only missing one Treasure. For example, facing a 2500% Star Peng with 1400% Treasures instead of 1500% results in him having '''700k''' health and '''37.5k''' damage.

==Strategy==
Star Pengs are often spammed and heavily buffed, so you will want to rely on [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]], especially those with crowd-control abilities like [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], as his low range leaves him vulnerable. [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat Mk II]] makes for a great meatshield with its [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] abilities and Warp immunity, and later on you can sometimes rely on [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] to stall him. Other [[:Category:Cats with Warp Immunity|Warp-immune Cats]] are also good to bring, as Star Peng by then won't be able to abuse its ability, but make sure they also have something that allows them to deal with him. Units from the [[Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES (Gacha Event)|ELEMENTAL PIXIES]] set are often more than a match and can greatly assist the fight against Star Peng.

